[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (3 issue(s)) — The implementation correctly addresses AC1 (preview_token, not management_token), AC2 (no host inside live_preview block), AC5/AC6 (prior review feedback fully addressed, src/interface/contentstack.ts actually edited), and AC4 (tests exist at the correct pre-existing path with all three required scenarios plus extras). However, AC3 is only partially met: while the `live_preview` field was added to `ICommonContentstackConfig` and `setCommonConfig` does destructure and forward it, the `content_type_uid` needed by `livePreviewQuery` is extracted from the query object via `(query as any).content_type_uid` — a property that exists only in the test mock (which was specifically modified to set it) but not on the real SDK's Query instance. This will cause `livePreviewQuery` to receive `content_type_uid: undefined` in production, silently breaking per-query live preview. Additionally, the pagination loop in `getEntry` drops `live_preview` for subsequent pages. The fix is straightforward: pass `contentTypeUid` explicitly to `setCommonConfig` and include `live_preview` in the pagination loop.

