[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (6 issue(s)) — The change correctly addresses AC1 (preview_token, not management_token), AC2 (no host inside live_preview block), and AC6 (src/interface/contentstack.ts was edited directly). Tests exist at the correct path (AC4). However, two blocker-level runtime defects remain: (1) setCommonConfig extracts content_type_uid from the Query object via an unsafe cast to contentstack.Entry — Query objects don't expose this property, so livePreviewQuery will never be called at runtime; the contentTypeUid should be passed through from createContentTypeQuery instead. (2) The live_preview forwarding condition requires both `preview_hash` and `live_preview` inner fields to be truthy, which is redundant and will silently skip live preview when callers provide only preview_hash. Both issues mean the core feature — draft content flowing through to queries — will silently fail at runtime despite tests passing (the tests mock content_type_uid on the fake query and set both fields to the same value, masking the defects).

