[0;32m[PASS][0m   Review: approved — The implementation correctly addresses all prior review feedback and meets the acceptance criteria: (1) The Stack options use `preview_token` (not management_token) with `enable: true` when CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN is set; (2) No `host` field is added inside the live_preview block — host is handled separately via Stack.setHost with correct priority (CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST takes priority over CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST); (3) ICommonContentstackConfig in src/interface/contentstack.ts gains an optional `live_preview` field of type IContentstackLivePreviewConfig, and setCommonConfig destructures it and forwards preview_hash to queries via `query.addParam('live_preview', preview_hash)`; (4) Five new vitest tests are added to the existing src/services/__tests__/contentstack.spec.ts file covering: live_preview block present with preview_token, live_preview absent when token unset, setHost priority with preview host, setHost fallback to API host, setHost not called when neither host set, plus two forwarding tests for getEntry and getSingleEntry verifying addParam is called with the correct hash and not called when preview_hash is absent. TypeScript strict compliance is maintained — no new untyped `any` introduced in production code. The change is concise (minimal diff) and reuses the existing ContentstackFactory/setCommonConfig pattern rather than hand-rolling new logic. One major finding: findSingletonEntry and getSingletonEntry do not forward live_preview, which will cause live preview to silently fail for singleton content types.

