[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (2 issue(s)) — The implementation correctly addresses AC1, AC2, AC3, AC4, AC5, and AC6. The live_preview block uses preview_token (not management_token) with enable:true, no host field inside the block, the ICommonContentstackConfig interface was edited in-scope to add the live_preview field, setCommonConfig forwards preview_hash via query.addParam('live_preview', hash), and 5 new vitest tests cover all required scenarios (23 total tests, all passing). All 4 prior review defects are resolved. However, two major findings remain: findSingletonEntry (line 305) and getSingletonEntry (line 354) accept live_preview via their interface (IContentstackGetSingletonEntry extends ICommonContentstackConfig) but do not destructure or forward it to createContentTypeQuery, silently dropping preview context for those code paths. getSingletonEntry is the most heavily used query function in the codebase (20+ call sites across pageService, stationService, userAccountService, and multiple page components), so this gap affects the majority of content fetches. These should be fixed to ensure all query paths support draft preview for linked/tabular references.

